WEBVTT

01:14.800 --> 01:16.640
The true forms

01:16.390 --> 01:16.640
Of the things that I gazed at

01:18.270 --> 01:18.520
Were for showing after I closed my eyes

01:19.310 --> 01:22.190
Shigofumi

01:21.980 --> 01:22.230
Again today, time

01:23.810 --> 01:24.060
Will only construct a loneliness

01:25.610 --> 01:25.860
That seems to be torn apart, right?

01:33.030 --> 01:33.280
There are people who can't forget about

01:36.700 --> 01:36.950
The white lotuses that bloom in the darkness

01:40.330 --> 01:40.580
Nevertheless, recollections

01:44.080 --> 01:44.330
Visit from the future

01:47.750 --> 01:48.000
Words that turn into sighs

01:55.180 --> 01:55.430
Are the emerging wings of the soul

01:58.850 --> 01:59.100
Will I flutter apart?

02:02.560 --> 02:02.810
Growing confused and disordered

02:06.230 --> 02:06.480
I want to carve

02:08.570 --> 02:08.820
These letters to you

02:13.570 --> 02:13.820
Pieces of the truth

02:15.410 --> 02:15.660
Of things that I want to tell you-

02:17.280 --> 02:17.530
I can't even send them well to you

02:21.040 --> 02:21.290
If I write them with the blood that stains my fingertips

02:24.710 --> 02:24.960
Then can they spill into your heart?

02:28.380 --> 02:28.630
Even if the one word left behind

02:31.880 --> 02:34.550
To us who live

02:34.300 --> 02:34.550
Is to be goodbye

02:42.600 --> 02:45.100
You know, when you're standing on the platform at the station...

02:45.560 --> 02:48.020
don't you have things that cross your mind?

02:49.190 --> 02:51.570
Like, what would happen if you jumped?

02:52.190 --> 02:53.190
Or something?

02:53.490 --> 02:54.700
Never.

02:54.700 --> 02:56.570
Whoa, an immediate reply.

02:56.570 --> 02:58.530
Kotake, you want to kill yourself?

02:58.530 --> 03:01.830
Bullied? Or problem with your parents?

03:01.830 --> 03:03.000
That's not it.

03:03.000 --> 03:05.920
It's not that I want to die. I'm talking about jumping.

03:05.920 --> 03:07.460
Isn't that the same?

03:07.460 --> 03:10.460
Normally, you'd die if you jumped in front of a train.

03:10.460 --> 03:14.550
Well, of course. But, that's not what I'm trying to say.

03:15.760 --> 03:17.800
Ah, I get it!

03:17.800 --> 03:19.970
That's Sen-chan for you!

03:19.970 --> 03:22.810
You never thought of killing yourself, right, Kaname?

03:22.810 --> 03:23.980
So that's what you're getting at?

03:23.980 --> 03:25.640
Nope. That's obvious, isn't it?

03:26.100 --> 03:27.810
What about you, Sen-chan?

03:27.810 --> 03:29.610
Ever thought of killing yourself?

03:34.900 --> 03:35.570
Nope.

03:35.570 --> 03:37.160
What was that?

03:37.160 --> 03:38.700
Don't scare us like that.

03:39.200 --> 03:41.330
It's because you're saying such weird things.

03:41.330 --> 03:42.330
Is it weird?

03:42.330 --> 03:45.960
It's certainly strange. You don't
have any reason to want to die either.

03:45.960 --> 03:47.120
Ehh?

03:47.120 --> 03:48.460
What do you think, Sen-chan?

03:48.460 --> 03:48.960
Huh?

03:49.960 --> 03:51.090
I...

03:52.000 --> 03:53.590
Sen-chan!

03:54.510 --> 03:56.380
Maki is calling for you.

03:56.380 --> 03:58.010
Oh, really?

03:59.510 --> 04:00.430
What is it?

04:00.430 --> 04:01.180
Class cleaning duty.

04:09.190 --> 04:11.020
Sen-chan!

04:11.020 --> 04:12.400
Right, right.

04:13.230 --> 04:14.780
I'm going.

04:14.780 --> 04:17.360
Geez, I already told you this morning.

04:17.360 --> 04:18.110
Really?

04:18.110 --> 04:20.070
Quit playing dumb.

04:21.740 --> 04:23.240
He seems like the type that always forgets.

04:23.620 --> 04:26.370
That's because you remember too many things, Kaname.

04:26.370 --> 04:28.500
Better than forgetting, right?

04:28.500 --> 04:34.250
People can live because they forget sad
and embarrassing moments in their life.

04:34.750 --> 04:37.050
That's quoted from somewhere, isn't it?

04:37.050 --> 04:37.840
Am I that easy to figure out?

04:38.510 --> 04:40.800
You know the game I cleared the other day...

04:53.900 --> 04:55.820
This stage is hard.

05:04.200 --> 05:05.280
What is it, Kaname?

05:05.280 --> 05:06.870
<i>Kotake, did you hear?</i>

05:06.870 --> 05:08.410
Did a plane crash?

05:08.410 --> 05:10.540
Or did the school burn down?

05:10.540 --> 05:12.710
<i>Don't be stupid. It's not that.</i>

05:13.210 --> 05:14.840
<i>Sen-chan is dead.</i>

05:19.340 --> 05:21.840
Don't think you can get away with your host-like attitude!

05:21.840 --> 05:23.970
Sorry! I'm really sorry!

05:23.970 --> 05:25.930
You destroyed our merchandise!

05:25.930 --> 05:27.390
You think an apology will cut it?

05:27.390 --> 05:29.390
How could anything good come from killing her? Bastard!

05:30.230 --> 05:31.190
Wait.

05:39.030 --> 05:40.860
My job comes first.

05:40.860 --> 05:41.900
Job?

05:41.900 --> 05:43.780
You're not allowed in here.

05:43.780 --> 05:45.320
Get out now!

05:45.950 --> 05:46.780
Why you!

05:47.700 --> 05:49.040
You...!

06:00.920 --> 06:03.010
Thank you for saving me.

06:03.010 --> 06:04.260
You're strong.

06:04.550 --> 06:06.220
That was really amazing.

06:07.850 --> 06:09.770
You've got mail!

06:10.930 --> 06:12.180
A letter?

06:12.180 --> 06:15.650
A Shigofumi. A letter from the world of the departed.

06:16.610 --> 06:18.270
That's interesting.

06:18.270 --> 06:20.030
So, who is it from?

06:20.030 --> 06:21.280
I hope it's from someone pretty.

06:24.570 --> 06:25.740
What is...?

06:26.530 --> 06:29.620
I've told you. It's from the world of the departed.

06:29.620 --> 06:30.910
Right, Daddy?

06:31.250 --> 06:33.410
My work here is done.

06:35.580 --> 06:38.630
W-Wait. Weren't you here to help me?

06:39.170 --> 06:41.010
I'm a postal worker.

06:41.010 --> 06:43.050
Saving others isn't part of my job.

06:49.430 --> 06:51.100
Poor thing.

06:51.100 --> 06:52.350
He got what he deserved.

06:52.350 --> 06:55.350
You would think that the girl who
got cheated on would be the fool, right?

06:55.350 --> 06:57.270
But, something like that...

07:00.650 --> 07:01.980
From the Gospel Department?

07:01.980 --> 07:05.610
Yeah. It looks like another person has died.

07:06.820 --> 07:07.820
I see.

07:14.080 --> 07:18.170
He didn't leave a suicide note or
anything on the apartment rooftop?

07:18.790 --> 07:22.340
Well, I can't understand the
feelings of someone who wants to die.

07:22.340 --> 07:25.550
They should just run away from the things they hate.

07:25.550 --> 07:27.680
It's not something to kill yourself over.

07:31.350 --> 07:33.600
You know Senkawa Daiki-kun, don't you?

07:33.980 --> 07:36.020
Was he ever bullied?

07:39.730 --> 07:41.270
What time will this news broadcast be?

07:41.730 --> 07:44.150
I have to record this for my parents.

07:51.330 --> 07:53.950
Hey, you there. Can I have a moment of your time?

07:57.460 --> 08:00.920
That's horrible, Sen-chan.
How could you kill yourself like that?

08:00.920 --> 08:03.170
And we were his friends too.

08:03.170 --> 08:05.460
I would have liked to talked things through with him.

08:06.380 --> 08:07.590
Friends?

08:08.760 --> 08:10.050
Were we really?

08:10.550 --> 08:11.680
Kotake.

08:12.470 --> 08:14.720
You're up next.

08:14.720 --> 08:15.350
For what?

08:15.810 --> 08:18.060
The principals are calling.

08:18.890 --> 08:22.310
This could jeopardise the reputation of the school!

08:22.310 --> 08:26.440
Please tell us what you know.
It's a student's responsibility to inform us.

08:26.440 --> 08:28.820
You were close to him, weren't you?!

08:28.820 --> 08:31.070
Why did Senkawa die?!

08:32.780 --> 08:35.410
Anything will do. Please, just talk.

08:39.920 --> 08:42.380
<i>So, you really have no idea?</i>

08:42.380 --> 08:46.130
<i>Yeah. There were never any problems in our household.</i>

08:46.460 --> 08:51.590
<i>I suspect Daiki's death must be due to some problem in school.</i>

08:52.010 --> 08:53.220
Really?

08:53.220 --> 08:55.060
Why are you asking me?

08:55.060 --> 08:57.430
Well, because Sen-chan is your friend, right?

08:57.430 --> 08:58.770
Yours too.

08:59.480 --> 09:01.270
You think so?

09:01.900 --> 09:07.360
The teachers and others from the class asked
me a lot of questions regarding Sen-chan's death.

09:07.360 --> 09:10.070
But, I couldn't answer any of their questions.

09:11.030 --> 09:18.120
Come to think of it, I know nothing of
Sen-chan's family structure, his ambitions, his dreams...

09:18.540 --> 09:22.750
I was thinking... we just hung out
together, but were never really friends.

09:24.000 --> 09:25.250
That's normal, isn't it?

09:25.250 --> 09:26.050
Eh?

09:26.050 --> 09:30.670
It's normal to not know what
that guy is ever really thinking.

09:30.670 --> 09:31.260
But...

09:31.760 --> 09:33.510
During middle school...

09:33.510 --> 09:36.810
a girl from my class suddenly shot her father.

09:36.810 --> 09:37.720
Huh?

09:37.720 --> 09:40.850
They were actually very close.

09:41.390 --> 09:46.070
But, I never imagined that she would ever do such a thing.

09:46.070 --> 09:47.270
Even now.

09:48.900 --> 09:50.950
Guess it's something we'll never understand.

09:50.950 --> 09:55.910
Yeah, we'll never understand another's thoughts.

09:59.250 --> 10:00.700
Honestly!

10:00.700 --> 10:04.330
Why do people do things like kill themselves?

10:04.920 --> 10:07.250
Whatever happened to their survival instincts?

10:08.050 --> 10:12.260
Isn't this what they call "desecration of life"?

10:12.970 --> 10:14.260
It's because they're broken.

10:14.260 --> 10:14.970
Huh?

10:15.260 --> 10:17.140
Humans are broken.

10:17.140 --> 10:20.390
Suicide, incest, parenticide.

10:20.980 --> 10:24.400
The only creatures with so many flaws are humans.

10:24.400 --> 10:26.480
Yeah, you're right.

10:26.480 --> 10:29.150
Humans sure are strange.

10:44.210 --> 10:48.380
<i>Next up: news regarding the
mysterious suicide of Senkawa Daiki-kun.</i>

10:48.790 --> 10:51.010
<i>No suicide note was left behind, was there?</i>

10:51.010 --> 10:52.760
<i>Any possibility of it being an accident?</i>

10:52.760 --> 10:54.550
<i>This is definitely a case of bullying.</i>

10:54.550 --> 10:58.800
<i>It's a fact that schools often fail to
grasp the severity of a student's situation.</i>

10:58.800 --> 11:01.770
<i>There are also rumours about domestic violence.</i>

11:01.770 --> 11:04.520
<i>This is clearly a case of Apathy Syndrome.</i>

11:04.810 --> 11:08.020
<i>It's like nothing will come from living. Growing up...</i>

11:10.980 --> 11:12.480
They're all wrong.

11:13.030 --> 11:15.360
None of those fit Sen-chan's character.

11:18.070 --> 11:19.450
Then, why?

11:20.160 --> 11:23.580
There's no reason for Sen-chan to take his own life.

11:32.630 --> 11:36.800
Yeah, we'll never understand another's thoughts.

11:38.640 --> 11:40.260
We might not understand.

11:40.850 --> 11:43.180
But, wouldn't people want to understand?

11:47.810 --> 11:48.850
Who is he?

11:48.850 --> 11:49.690
A teacher?

11:49.690 --> 11:51.480
No one move!

11:59.070 --> 12:03.120
This place is now a courtroom!

12:03.120 --> 12:05.120
Shigofumi

12:06.210 --> 12:08.210
Shigofumi

12:08.540 --> 12:14.800
The father of suicide victim, Senkawa Daiki-kun, is
currently holding students hostage in a classroom.

12:15.090 --> 12:17.380
Gunshots have been confirmed.

12:16.800 --> 12:19.970
Please stay calm. Those with family inside please come this way.

12:17.930 --> 12:21.550
According to the mother, the father,
overwhelmed by the loss of Daiki-kun...

12:23.220 --> 12:27.940
I just want to know the reason behind my son's death.

12:29.400 --> 12:31.150
You all can understand, can't you?

12:36.070 --> 12:38.530
You will talk, won't you?

12:38.530 --> 12:39.700
About Daiki.

12:42.530 --> 12:44.870
Did anything happen to my son before?

12:44.870 --> 12:47.580
I don't know anything.

12:48.040 --> 12:51.210
He couldn't have possibly died without reason.

12:51.500 --> 12:54.130
But, he was never bullied.

12:54.130 --> 12:57.090
It's true! Sen-chan was always so cheerful!

12:57.630 --> 13:01.050
Folks, please comply with the
instructions from the police officers.

13:01.050 --> 13:03.350
This might provoke the perpetrator.

13:04.180 --> 13:05.060
Noji-san?

13:05.720 --> 13:07.350
Are you our backup?

13:08.060 --> 13:09.350
Negative.

13:09.350 --> 13:11.730
My son is held inside.

13:11.730 --> 13:12.400
Eh?

13:17.320 --> 13:18.070
Hey, you!

13:21.410 --> 13:22.450
What's the matter?

13:23.120 --> 13:25.450
No, it's nothing.

13:26.200 --> 13:28.330
Then, let me change my question.

13:29.250 --> 13:32.290
Who was my son closest to?

13:33.210 --> 13:35.130
That person is inside this classroom, right?

13:43.890 --> 13:45.850
Sen-chan is dead.

13:46.350 --> 13:48.890
He jumped from the rooftop of his apartment building.

13:54.650 --> 13:55.980
What are you trying to pull?

13:58.730 --> 14:01.150
Sen-chan told us...

14:01.860 --> 14:03.910
that he never thought about dying.

14:06.870 --> 14:08.370
It was this afternoon.

14:09.120 --> 14:11.120
Not even half a day has passed since then.

14:11.710 --> 14:12.710
Why?

14:18.250 --> 14:21.550
<i>What about you, Sen-chan? Ever thought of killing yourself?</i>

14:22.590 --> 14:23.550
Nope.

14:25.010 --> 14:26.220
Is it you?

14:26.220 --> 14:26.970
Huh?

14:27.850 --> 14:31.140
You were close to my son, weren't you?

14:31.140 --> 14:32.230
Thank you.

14:32.230 --> 14:34.060
Ah, not at all.

14:34.060 --> 14:36.110
You would know, wouldn't you?

14:36.110 --> 14:39.020
The person who caused Daiki's death.

14:40.980 --> 14:42.490
I don't know.

14:45.910 --> 14:48.330
Are you covering for someone?

14:48.330 --> 14:50.870
Or are you worried about your student record?

14:51.370 --> 14:54.580
As Daiki's friend, won't you tell me?

14:55.370 --> 14:56.630
Friend...

14:56.630 --> 15:02.510
As Daiki's friend, you wouldn't let the
person who killed Daiki go unpunished, would you?

15:03.380 --> 15:06.470
Why did Sen-chan die?

15:06.470 --> 15:06.930
What?

15:07.390 --> 15:09.600
Even you, the father, don't know?

15:10.680 --> 15:12.390
Do you not know?

15:12.390 --> 15:14.140
Stop it, Kotake!

15:14.140 --> 15:16.060
I want to know as well!

15:16.060 --> 15:18.310
I want to know why Sen-chan died.

15:18.310 --> 15:21.110
Sorry, he's extremely upset over Daiki-kun's death...

15:21.110 --> 15:22.650
It wasn't me!

15:24.780 --> 15:27.740
I never abused him.

15:27.740 --> 15:30.280
I... I...

15:40.420 --> 15:42.960
Two hours have passed since the start of the hostage situation.

15:43.300 --> 15:46.550
But, we still have no word as to the hostage taker's demands.

15:52.100 --> 15:55.060
Forgive us, Noji-san. We had to remain on standby.

15:55.060 --> 15:59.150
Not at all. We can't do anything without the superiors here.

16:02.070 --> 16:03.400
Kaname...

16:05.150 --> 16:07.820
<i>This is Metropolitan Police Defence
Force Department, First Defence Force.</i>

16:08.490 --> 16:11.950
<i>Spec-ops raid unit 24. We're in position.</i>

16:11.950 --> 16:12.990
Roger.

16:16.120 --> 16:17.330
Now...

16:18.750 --> 16:20.540
You... are?

16:21.790 --> 16:22.790
Who are you?

16:23.250 --> 16:26.300
I deliver Shigofumis.

16:26.970 --> 16:28.300
Shigofumis?

16:29.260 --> 16:31.720
Letters from the world of the departed.

16:32.180 --> 16:33.350
Departed?

16:34.060 --> 16:34.850
You mean...?

16:35.180 --> 16:38.190
The sender is Senkawa Daiki.

16:39.310 --> 16:42.020
It's addressed to Kotake Tohru.

16:42.520 --> 16:43.610
For me?

16:44.320 --> 16:45.820
From Sen-chan?

16:46.110 --> 16:46.990
Wait!

16:47.280 --> 16:49.360
If it's a letter from Daiki, then let me read it.

16:52.120 --> 16:53.700
What is it?

16:54.950 --> 16:56.660
Don't you dare!

16:56.660 --> 16:58.290
The letter is for me.

16:58.290 --> 17:00.540
That letter is from my son!

17:00.540 --> 17:02.170
It's addressed to me.

17:02.460 --> 17:03.880
Quiet!

17:13.930 --> 17:15.470
It can't be...

17:16.220 --> 17:19.230
My job involves the safe delivery of Shigofumis.

17:19.850 --> 17:20.850
Do not interfere.

17:42.420 --> 17:43.880
W-Wait!

17:46.880 --> 17:49.420
Please read it aloud.

17:49.420 --> 17:51.170
I wish to know as well.

17:54.300 --> 17:55.680
Very well.

17:57.680 --> 17:59.020
Kotake,

18:00.060 --> 18:02.140
this isn't something very important.

18:02.890 --> 18:06.570
But, since I've been given this special
privilege, I was told to write a few words.

18:08.650 --> 18:12.280
We never finished our talk on the rooftop, did we?

18:12.950 --> 18:15.030
It lingered in my mind.

18:15.700 --> 18:18.330
I've thought about it too.

18:18.330 --> 18:21.200
About what it'd be like to jump.

18:21.960 --> 18:24.370
We all get that feeling, right?

18:25.290 --> 18:27.590
It's not that I want to die or anything.

18:28.170 --> 18:30.550
But, I guess it's not about wanting to live either.

18:51.610 --> 18:52.740
I see.

18:52.740 --> 18:56.530
All Sen-chan did was jump.

18:57.240 --> 18:58.700
That's why he died.

18:59.490 --> 19:02.620
I too, sometimes wonder what would happen if I jumped.

19:13.420 --> 19:15.300
There was no real reason.

19:16.640 --> 19:19.100
I just decided to pick a different path.

19:19.100 --> 19:21.640
Just like how I chose to have a yakisoba bun for lunch.

19:22.560 --> 19:25.810
I just felt that way at the time.

19:28.900 --> 19:30.440
It can't be!

19:39.910 --> 19:42.330
Give me that! It must be a fake.

19:42.330 --> 19:45.830
My Daiki would never write this letter.

19:45.830 --> 19:46.870
This piece of...

19:46.870 --> 19:47.830
This piece of...

19:47.830 --> 19:48.710
It's authentic.

19:48.710 --> 19:49.710
What?

19:49.710 --> 19:52.590
Sen-chan wrote it.

19:53.090 --> 19:54.720
There's no mistaking it.

19:54.720 --> 19:56.170
How do you know?

19:56.550 --> 19:57.590
Because...

20:11.730 --> 20:13.690
<i>The target has been apprehended.</i>

20:13.690 --> 20:15.150
Are there any casualties?

20:15.150 --> 20:16.400
<i>Confirming.</i>

20:17.320 --> 20:18.660
<i>Everyone is safe.</i>

20:21.580 --> 20:24.080
Daiki would never have taken his own life!

20:24.080 --> 20:25.750
He's not that kind of kid!

20:26.040 --> 20:27.120
He's not that kind of kid!

20:27.120 --> 20:28.580
He's not that kind of kid!

20:34.550 --> 20:37.050
Because, I'm his friend.

20:38.180 --> 20:42.550
Sen-chan, is it okay for me to be your friend?

20:49.690 --> 20:51.690
"Death brings not salvation -

20:51.690 --> 20:53.480
only evanescence."

20:53.770 --> 20:55.190
What in the world was that?

20:55.190 --> 20:56.990
Mikawa Kirameki.

20:56.990 --> 20:59.650
It's a quote from a popular novelist some time ago.

20:59.650 --> 21:00.820
Hmm...

21:00.820 --> 21:01.950
Mikawa!

21:02.700 --> 21:04.030
Mikawa.

21:04.030 --> 21:05.160
Mikawa, it's you, isn't it?

21:08.710 --> 21:09.620
Who's he?

21:10.210 --> 21:14.170
It's me, your classmate from
Year 2 of middle school, Nojima Kaname.

21:14.420 --> 21:15.090
Huh?

21:16.670 --> 21:18.510
Mikawa, why did you...?

21:19.420 --> 21:21.680
Why did you shoot your own father?!

21:21.970 --> 21:23.010
Ehh?!

21:51.250 --> 21:56.090
Shigofumi

21:51.250 --> 21:56.090
Episode Three

21:51.250 --> 21:56.090
Friends

23:26.970 --> 23:28.600
I loved her.

23:28.890 --> 23:30.430
I admired her.

23:31.100 --> 23:35.810
Was it hatred or love which I saw
at the end of those feelings I held?

23:36.850 --> 23:38.900
Next time on Shigofumi:

23:39.230 --> 23:41.230
Shigofumi

23:39.230 --> 23:41.230
Episode Four

23:39.230 --> 23:41.230
Tears
